<title>UK: Brands Hatch shares show debut premium.</title>
<headline>Brands Hatch shares show debut premium.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-11-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in racing track operator Brands Hatch Leisure Plc showed a 13 percent premium on their first day of trading on the London Stock Exchange on Thursday.</p>
<p>By 1600 GMT the shares were quoted at 177-1/2p, 20-1/2p above the 157p placing price, with some 1.2 million shares traded. The placing valued the company at 34.3 million stg.</p>
<p>&quot;The flotation represents a major step in our company's development,&quot; said chief executive Nicola Foulston.</p>
<p>The 9.3 million stg raised by the issue, sponsored by Beeson Gregory, will be used to reduce borrowings and to invest in capital projects.</p>
<p>-- John Sutherland, London Newsroom, +44 171 542 7945</p>
</text>
